{
 "version": 8,
 "name": "Satellite",
 "metadata": {
  "gpui-maps:note": "Imagery basemap. Deliberately carries NO fill or line layer: a vector water/land polygon would paint over the imagery it is meant to sit under. Labels and boundaries only. The one exception is the `background` layer, which is BEHIND the raster pass rather than over it (render_with_space_and_raster draws the backdrop, then raster, then the vector layers) and exists so a tile that has not arrived reads as unloaded ground rather than as a black hole.",
  "gpui-maps:labels": "White ink on a tight neutral dark halo, no blur. Liberty's own label layers are dark text on a white halo, which is correct over a pale vector map and exactly backwards over imagery -- copying them verbatim is what made a water label read as mid-blue under a white glow."
 },
